# ncly-{{ slug }}

`ncly-{{ slug }}` is an extension of [Nicely](https://github.com/pascalandy/nicely), which adds `ncly {{ root }}`{% if not name %} and the commands beneath it{% endif %}.
`vision.md` states its job, and `spec.md` states what each command proves.

## Install

A release installs with `ncly`, Go, and `just`.
To install `ncly`, follow Install in [Nicely's README](https://github.com/pascalandy/nicely#install).
Replace TAG with a release tag, such as `v0.1.0`. `git ls-remote --tags https://{{ module }}` lists the tags.

```sh
git clone --branch TAG https://{{ module }} ncly-{{ slug }}
cd ncly-{{ slug }}
just install
ncly describe {{ root }} --json
```

For an annotated tag, Git can warn that the tag `is not a commit!`, then note a detached HEAD: the clone holds the tagged commit.
`ncly describe` confirms the install, with `{{ root }}` and the source `extension`.
`just install` replaces a previous install, and grants no key.
An agent reads `ncly skill view {{ slug }}` to learn when to use the extension.

